## Why This Is Asked

This question tests ability to design cost-aware prompt orchestration, a practical constraint in cloud analytics workflows.

## Key Concepts

- Token cost estimation
- Budget-constrained orchestration
- Module selection strategy
- Latency-awareness

## Code Example

```javascript
function estimateTokens(prompt, overhead = 20) {
  return prompt.split(/\s+/).length + overhead;
}

function selectModules(prompt, budget, candidates) {
  let total = 0;
  const chosen = [];
  for (const [name, cost] of candidates) {
    if (total + cost <= budget) {
      chosen.push(name);
      total += cost;
    }
  }
  return chosen;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you refine costs with real model pricing?
- How handle dynamic budgets or partial module failures?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to extend routing with governance constraints and to design testable prototypes.

## Key Concepts
- multi-module routing with governance
- signal design: intent, data_sensitivity, governance_policy
- edge-case handling: conflicts, missing role

## Code Example
```javascript
function route(prompt, signals){
  if (signals.governance_policy === 'restrict') return {module:'Data-Governance', payload:{prompt}};
  if (signals.data_sensitivity === 'PII') return {module:'PII-redactor', payload:{prompt}};
  return {module:'SQL-builder', payload:{prompt}};
}
module.exports = route;
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you unit test the routing logic for edge cases like conflicting signals?
- How would you extend the router to support additional governance policies without breaking existing behavior?

